*> Implementation test of client/src/net-client.cob (NET-ADDRESS-PARSE, NET-OPEN, NET-PUMP,
*> NET-SEND, NET-CLOSE, NET-FAIL; contracts/shim-abi.md §3; client-surface.md §2; research R14)
*> against a loopback listener the test opens and serves fixture bytes from: address parsing
*> (host, host:port, default 25565); a status exchange over a real non-blocking connection; a
*> refused connection, an unresolved host, a lost connection and malformed data each log
*> "ERROR connection: <detail>" and return the Player to the server list (a status connection
*> marks its entry unreachable).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-NET-CLIENT.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 COPY CLCONST.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-ADDRESS             PIC X(256).
 01 WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH      BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HOST                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-HOST-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-PORT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CONN                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NEXT                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-ONE                 BINARY-LONG VALUE 1.
 01 WS-WAIT                BINARY-LONG VALUE 50.
 01 WS-LISTENER            BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-SERVER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-RC                  BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-HANDLES.
    05 WS-HANDLE           BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-READY               PIC X(2).
 01 WS-PATH                PIC X(256).
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-THRESHOLD           BINARY-LONG VALUE -1.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC Z(5)9.
 01 WS-GARBAGE             PIC X(4) VALUE X"FFFFFFFF".
 01 WS-FOUR                BINARY-LONG VALUE 4.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     CALL "CL-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "PACK-STACK-INIT" USING CLIENT-STATE
     CALL "LANG-LOAD" USING CLIENT-STATE

     MOVE "example.org" TO WS-ADDRESS
     MOVE 11 TO WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH
     CALL "NET-ADDRESS-PARSE" USING WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-HOST WS-HOST-LENGTH WS-PORT
     MOVE "net client address host alone: port 25565" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "example.org 25565" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-PORT TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-HOST(1:WS-HOST-LENGTH) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "localhost:25570" TO WS-ADDRESS
     MOVE 15 TO WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH
     CALL "NET-ADDRESS-PARSE" USING WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-HOST WS-HOST-LENGTH WS-PORT
     MOVE "net client address host:port" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "localhost 25570" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-PORT TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING WS-HOST(1:WS-HOST-LENGTH) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   A status exchange with a loopback server serving fixture bytes.
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_listen" USING BY VALUE WS-ZERO BY REFERENCE WS-LISTENER
         BY REFERENCE WS-PORT RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE WS-PORT TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-ADDRESS
     STRING "127.0.0.1:" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-ADDRESS
     MOVE FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-ADDRESS)) TO WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH
     MOVE 1 TO SL-COUNT
     MOVE CONN-PING TO WS-CONN
     MOVE 1 TO CN-ENTRY(WS-CONN)
     MOVE PH-STATUS TO WS-NEXT
     CALL "NET-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-NEXT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) NOT = PH-CONNECTING OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
     MOVE WS-LISTENER TO WS-HANDLE
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_poll" USING BY VALUE WS-WAIT BY REFERENCE WS-HANDLES BY VALUE WS-ONE
         BY VALUE WS-ZERO BY REFERENCE WS-READY RETURNING WS-RC
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_accept" USING BY VALUE WS-LISTENER BY REFERENCE WS-SERVER
         RETURNING WS-RC
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "net client a status connection completes its connect and sends Intention and Status "
         & "Request" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "00 00" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     MOVE "contract/fixtures/wire/status-s2c-00-status-response.hex" TO WS-PATH
     CALL "TEST-SERVE" USING WS-SERVER WS-PATH WS-THRESHOLD
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL SL-DESC-LENGTH(1) > 0 OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
     CALL "TEST-SERVER-READ" USING WS-SERVER WS-TEXT WS-THRESHOLD
     MOVE "net client received bytes are framed into packets: the Status Response fills the entry "
         & "and Ping Request goes out" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "A CobolCraft server 01" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     STRING SL-DESC(1)(1:SL-DESC-LENGTH(1)) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The server goes away during the exchange: the entry is unreachable.
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_close" USING BY VALUE WS-SERVER
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) = PH-NONE OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "net client a status connection lost before Pong marks the entry unreachable" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "N" TO TL-MODE
     COMPUTE TL-EXPECTED-N = SLS-UNREACHABLE * 10 + PH-NONE
     COMPUTE TL-OBSERVED-N = SL-STATUS(1) * 10 + CN-PHASE(WS-CONN)
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   The game connection: malformed bytes in play.
     MOVE CONN-GAME TO WS-CONN
     MOVE PH-LOGIN TO WS-NEXT
     MOVE WS-ADDRESS TO SM-CONNECT-ADDR
     MOVE WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH TO SM-CONNECT-ADDR-LENGTH
     CALL "NET-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-NEXT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) NOT = PH-CONNECTING OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_poll" USING BY VALUE WS-WAIT BY REFERENCE WS-HANDLES BY VALUE WS-ONE
         BY VALUE WS-ZERO BY REFERENCE WS-READY RETURNING WS-RC
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_accept" USING BY VALUE WS-LISTENER BY REFERENCE WS-SERVER
         RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE PH-PLAY TO CN-PHASE(WS-CONN)
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO SM-SCREEN
     CALL "TEST-SERVE-BYTES" USING WS-SERVER WS-GARBAGE WS-FOUR
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) = PH-NONE OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "net client malformed data ends the connection and returns to the server list with "
         & "connecting.lost" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE "2 The connection was lost" TO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_close" USING BY VALUE WS-SERVER

*>   Lost in play: the server closes.
     CALL "NET-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-NEXT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) NOT = PH-CONNECTING OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_poll" USING BY VALUE WS-WAIT BY REFERENCE WS-HANDLES BY VALUE WS-ONE
         BY VALUE WS-ZERO BY REFERENCE WS-READY RETURNING WS-RC
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_accept" USING BY VALUE WS-LISTENER BY REFERENCE WS-SERVER
         RETURNING WS-RC
     MOVE SCR-WORLD TO SM-SCREEN
     MOVE 0 TO SM-MESSAGE-LENGTH
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_close" USING BY VALUE WS-SERVER
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) = PH-NONE OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "net client a connection the server closes ends with connecting.lost" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

*>   Refused: nothing listens on the port any more.
     CALL STATIC "cc_net_close" USING BY VALUE WS-LISTENER
     CALL "NET-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-NEXT
     PERFORM VARYING WS-I FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL CN-PHASE(WS-CONN) = PH-NONE OR WS-I > 100
         CALL "NET-PUMP" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN
         CALL "TEST-SLEEP"
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE "net client a refused connection returns to the server list with connecting.failed"
         TO TL-CASE
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED TL-EXPECTED
     STRING "2 Could not connect to " WS-ADDRESS(1:WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO TL-EXPECTED
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT

     MOVE "no.such.host.invalid" TO WS-ADDRESS SM-CONNECT-ADDR
     MOVE 20 TO WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH SM-CONNECT-ADDR-LENGTH
     MOVE SCR-CONNECTING TO SM-SCREEN
     CALL "NET-OPEN" USING CLIENT-STATE WS-CONN WS-ADDRESS WS-ADDRESS-LENGTH WS-NEXT
     MOVE "net client an unresolved host fails at once with connecting.failed" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "2 Could not connect to no.such.host.invalid" TO TL-EXPECTED
     MOVE SPACES TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE" USING CLIENT-STATE TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT
     STOP RUN.
 END PROGRAM TEST-NET-CLIENT.

 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC Z9.
 LINKAGE SECTION.
 COPY CLSTATE.
 01 L-TEXT                 PIC X(1024).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION USING CLIENT-STATE L-TEXT.
     MOVE SM-SCREEN TO WS-EDIT
     MOVE SPACES TO L-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) " " SM-MESSAGE(1:SM-MESSAGE-LENGTH) DELIMITED BY SIZE
         INTO L-TEXT
     GOBACK.
 END PROGRAM TEST-SCREEN-AND-MESSAGE.

 COPY CLTEST.
